From c03832c75c819e6808eedcea5a98326d4110831e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:12:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wow64win: convert audited win32u thunks through the iOS guest
 window

wow64win.dll takes the guest window's base from the TEB32/PEB32 pair,
as wow64.dll does, and converts through wow64_window.h: get_ptr,
put_addr and its string, object-attribute and security helpers, with
string buffers that may be atoms kept as atoms. Names and parameters
that are a pointer or a small integer (class and resource names,
properties, SystemParametersInfo values) convert only as pointers.
The NtUserCall*Param codes that take pointers convert them, and so do
class registration and lookup, cursor and icon data, bmBits and the
packed names in user callbacks. Procedures, instances, lpCreateParams,
resource handles and the DIB brush's client pointer stay guest values;
two handles read with get_ptr now use get_handle.

Only the thunks audited for this (window_audited.h: those whose
arguments are handles, integers or plain-data pointers, and the ones
converted here) run in a windowed process; any other win32u call ends
it, naming the call, which replaces wow64.dll's stop at the first
win32u call.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-03-portal2-wow64-pointers.md
Offered-upstream: no; the window exists only on the iOS port
